#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: elided
#> pause: 45
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> must:    [lines 2 to 4 elided]
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: Where Alph
#> not: pleasure dome
#> source: 2,4c\
# 9. i\ inserts before, c\ changes. McMahon 3.1
# i\ is a\ but writes its text before the line. c\ deletes the selected lines
# and writes its text once, even for a range: 2,4c\ replaces three lines with
# one. Leading blanks in the text would vanish (sed ignores them in commands);
# a backslash before the first blank keeps them, and does not appear itself.
# Try: change 2,4c\ to 2,4i\ and the three lines come back after the text.
2,4c\
\   [lines 2 to 4 elided]

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
